WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:03.730
<b>The</b>

00:01.150 --> 00:03.720
The bright red envelope is the key.

00:01.180 --> 00:03.730
<b>"bright
red
envelope" is 
the 
key.</b>

00:03.720 --> 00:10.650
So, where did the perpetrator get 
the envelope and the manuscript?

00:10.650 --> 00:12.350
The answer's simple.

00:13.280 --> 00:15.320
He killed and stole it...

00:15.650 --> 00:18.000
From the author himself.

01:48.420 --> 01:51.290
Hey, rival. What are you doing?

01:51.670 --> 01:53.960
Speed reading the manuscript.

01:53.960 --> 01:57.090
There might be something in 
here that could help Rampo-kun.

01:57.090 --> 02:01.050
Minoura-san, what exactly is this 
case of the mystery writer murder

02:01.050 --> 02:03.010
that everyone's talking about?

02:03.020 --> 02:04.680
What, you don't know?

02:04.720 --> 02:08.040
<b>Zuikaro</b>

02:05.090 --> 02:08.010
The body was discovered 
by the manager of the inn.

02:15.750 --> 02:16.960
What is that?

02:21.880 --> 02:25.650
The doll was carrying human ears.

02:26.080 --> 02:28.370
The author was an exceptionally 
talented detective novel writer.

02:28.890 --> 02:34.080
He was found murdered at the inn where 
he'd been staying long-term to work.

02:42.030 --> 02:45.670
The biggest mystery of this case is 
that the conditions around the murder

02:45.670 --> 02:48.480
resembled the murder depicted in the novel.

02:48.480 --> 02:52.940
That's the gist of the infamous 
Killing of Kindaichi.

02:50.350 --> 02:52.010
Gross...

02:52.780 --> 02:55.410
And I thought that I might find out

02:55.790 --> 03:00.240
who'd stolen the manuscript if 
I read the last chapter, but...

03:00.750 --> 03:05.630
<i>The murderer was an old acquaintance of the 
victim's, motivated by years of pent-up anger.</i>

03:05.630 --> 03:08.620
<i>It's exactly as Rampo-kun had deduced.</i>

03:09.120 --> 03:11.000
It was at that moment, when my colleague uttered those words,
that I became certain that a perfect murder does indeed exist.
End

03:09.700 --> 03:12.800
The word "End" on the last page is smudged.

03:13.690 --> 03:16.430
Are these water droplets?

03:16.430 --> 03:22.050
No, looking at it more carefully, 
it's not handwritten. It's a copy.

03:22.890 --> 03:23.970
Why?

03:27.780 --> 03:28.630
Well?

03:31.810 --> 03:36.070
<b>CAW CAW CAW CAW</b>

03:34.700 --> 03:36.450
What the hell?!

03:36.070 --> 03:37.980
<b>Beep</b>

03:38.410 --> 03:40.730
It's my cell phone.

03:40.730 --> 03:42.400
Why were you so surprised, then?

03:42.780 --> 03:45.610
I don't receive calls very often.

03:46.900 --> 03:47.910
What's this?!

03:48.420 --> 03:51.620
The evidence destroyer and the 
murderer are the same person?

03:51.920 --> 03:54.730
Don't you think that's a stretch?

03:54.730 --> 03:58.880
The manuscript could have been obtained 
by someone other than the murderer.

03:58.880 --> 04:00.540
I have evidence.

04:02.330 --> 04:04.090
This manuscript.

04:05.090 --> 04:07.600
End

04:05.100 --> 04:07.590
Why does he have the manuscript?!

04:07.830 --> 04:10.130
Looks like you recognize it, huh?

04:11.030 --> 04:14.100
It was folded up like this and hidden away,

04:14.450 --> 04:16.840
at the gift shop on the second 
floor of the observation deck.

04:17.200 --> 04:20.640
I checked inside the envelope 
as soon as I got it.

04:21.010 --> 04:23.990
And for some reason, just the 
last page was a photocopy.

04:24.520 --> 04:26.860
Was it so they could keep the original?

04:26.860 --> 04:29.840
No, in that case, they would 
have copied all the pages.

04:29.840 --> 04:31.330
That's when I realized...

04:31.730 --> 04:36.010
Maybe they printed it out in a hurry, 
right before it was handed off.

04:36.470 --> 04:39.750
So I checked a stationery shop nearby.

04:39.750 --> 04:42.970
And just as I expected, 
it was the same paper.

04:42.970 --> 04:45.710
In other words, the attacker was in a hurry 
to swap out the original with the copy.

04:45.710 --> 04:47.210
Why?

04:47.210 --> 04:49.810
If the content was an issue, 
they could have just thrown out that page.

04:50.380 --> 04:55.470
They didn't do that because there was a 
specific reason to hand over all the pages.

04:56.260 --> 05:00.710
If that's the case, the last page of the 
manuscript wouldn't have been thrown out.

05:00.710 --> 05:04.300
But they couldn't risk being searched, 
so they hid it somewhere.

05:05.070 --> 05:08.310
And so you found the hidden manuscript?

05:08.310 --> 05:12.990
As soon as I found it, I became certain the 
the same person was behind both incidents.

05:13.360 --> 05:14.830
By the way...

05:15.230 --> 05:16.850
What's your name?

05:16.850 --> 05:18.710
Oguri Mushitaro.

05:18.710 --> 05:20.050
Thanks.

05:20.050 --> 05:22.720
Now I have all the information I need.

05:23.710 --> 05:26.430
You're the one behind both of the incidents,

05:26.790 --> 05:28.990
Oguri Mushitaro-kun.

05:29.390 --> 05:32.390
Episode 42
A Perfect Murder
and Murderer (Part 2)

05:35.000 --> 05:36.200
Well, well...

05:36.200 --> 05:38.760
There are three types of cargo that I hate:

05:38.760 --> 05:40.600
Cargo that talks too much.

05:40.600 --> 05:42.810
Cargo that brings trouble.

05:42.810 --> 05:44.690
And cargo that doesn't pay.

05:45.080 --> 05:46.690
Anything to say for yourself?

05:46.690 --> 05:48.200
I've got nothing to say.

05:48.200 --> 05:50.070
He does, though.

05:50.070 --> 05:52.230
Put the gun away, getaway driver.

05:52.230 --> 05:53.790
Don't give the detectives any excuses.

05:54.650 --> 05:57.190
There is no direct evidence that 
will lead to our impeachment.

05:57.190 --> 05:59.480
He's never stood a chance to begin with.

05:59.480 --> 06:02.070
Unless you threaten him 
in plain sight, that is.

06:02.070 --> 06:04.880
He has no use for excuses when
 he's got a gun pointed at his head.

06:04.880 --> 06:06.310
Get out of the car.

06:06.310 --> 06:08.320
I don't want to get my seat dirty.

06:08.320 --> 06:10.340
Guns are fascinating, aren't they?

06:10.640 --> 06:13.330
For some reason, the moment you 
have one, you turn into an idiot.

06:13.910 --> 06:18.180
Sorry, but this situation was 
what I was going for all along.

06:18.180 --> 06:19.580
Drop the gun!

06:20.530 --> 06:22.280
Rampo-kun!

06:22.850 --> 06:25.740
I kept a call going with Poe-kun's phone.

06:23.980 --> 06:25.730
<b>E. Poe</b>

06:23.980 --> 06:25.730
<b>Disconnect</b>

06:23.980 --> 06:25.730
<b>Talk</b>

06:23.980 --> 06:25.730
<b>Mute</b>

06:30.670 --> 06:34.050
Such an anticlimactic end to 
the criminals of the century.

06:34.050 --> 06:35.630
I'll put you two in the same cell.

06:35.630 --> 06:36.870
You can hold a review session or something.

06:36.870 --> 06:37.870
Try.

06:38.840 --> 06:43.900
I am an official diplomat, and this 
car has foreign service plates.

06:43.900 --> 06:45.910
We have immunity from criminal law here.

06:46.420 --> 06:48.900
You can't arrest us.

06:49.880 --> 06:55.460
Still, an ongoing murder attempt should 
strip you of your privileges as a diplomat.

06:55.760 --> 06:57.670
It's not loaded.

06:57.670 --> 06:59.860
I can invoke what you lot call 
an impossibility defense.

06:59.860 --> 07:02.400
I was also granted the right 
to carry this pistol.

07:02.400 --> 07:03.610
There's no illegality in my using it.

07:03.880 --> 07:05.790
So the gun was an empty threat.

07:05.790 --> 07:07.520
Fyodor taught you that trick.

07:13.180 --> 07:14.550
You're free to go.

07:14.170 --> 07:14.550
Hey!

07:15.680 --> 07:17.480
So long, Rampo-kun.

07:17.480 --> 07:19.930
Say hi to your coworker in prison for me.

07:43.240 --> 07:45.950
<i>There's foreign text showing on the phone.</i>

07:46.480 --> 07:48.320
<i>This phone is...</i>

07:48.320 --> 07:50.490
<i>Mushitaro-kun, you win.</i>

07:51.490 --> 07:56.190
I've known all along: 
ordinary people can't defeat Gifted.

07:56.190 --> 07:58.870
Nevertheless, I'll defeat you...

07:59.450 --> 08:04.120
because my coworkers think I'm invincible.

08:06.120 --> 08:07.290
<i>Impossible...</i>

08:07.630 --> 08:09.370
<i>A special ability!</i>

08:12.940 --> 08:15.520
<i>I was certain he wasn't a Gifted...</i>

08:17.100 --> 08:18.380
<i>So dark...</i>

08:18.990 --> 08:20.390
<i>What just happened?</i>

08:20.720 --> 08:22.100
<i>I can't see anything.</i>

08:22.900 --> 08:24.020
<i>I can't breathe!</i>

08:24.020 --> 08:26.450
<i>Something's choking me!</i>

08:27.330 --> 08:28.350
<i>No...</i>

08:28.350 --> 08:29.110
<i>It's...</i>

08:30.480 --> 08:32.990
How could you kill me?!

08:32.990 --> 08:34.620
Yokomizo?!

08:34.620 --> 08:36.600
<i>What the hell is going on?</i>

08:37.090 --> 08:39.030
<i>This is the inn...</i>

08:39.550 --> 08:42.000
<i>where Yokomizo was murdered.</i>

08:42.000 --> 08:43.680
<i>But how?</i>

08:44.050 --> 08:46.220
<i>No, first...</i>

08:46.490 --> 08:47.990
I despise you!

08:47.990 --> 08:49.640
I despise you so!

08:50.370 --> 08:51.570
No!

08:52.160 --> 08:54.460
This isn't it, Yokomizo!

08:55.000 --> 08:56.170
Correct.

09:01.260 --> 09:03.130
This isn't reality.

09:03.420 --> 09:05.140
Reality looks like this.

09:07.850 --> 09:09.180
I see.

09:09.180 --> 09:11.350
This is the doing of the Guild's Gifted.

09:11.610 --> 09:13.740
We're inside Poe's novel.

09:14.440 --> 09:15.570
That's right.

09:16.260 --> 09:20.780
I sent out a message instructing him 
to reproduce the scene of the murder.

09:21.100 --> 09:22.300
I see.

09:22.570 --> 09:24.540
So that's what that text was.

09:24.970 --> 09:28.370
"This isn't it, Yokomizo," you said.

09:28.370 --> 09:30.700
You seem to be well-acquainted 
with the victim.

09:32.170 --> 09:35.120
Do you really think you've caught 
me with such a measly trap?

09:35.540 --> 09:38.510
As I said before, what you need is evidence.

09:38.790 --> 09:42.360
All your suspicions and 
deductions mean nothing.

09:42.360 --> 09:47.100
On top of that, 
you've made a critical mistake.

09:47.100 --> 09:48.110
A mistake?

09:48.110 --> 09:48.840
Yup.

09:48.840 --> 09:50.300
I looked up his profile.

09:50.780 --> 09:52.710
The Gifted author's special ability

09:52.710 --> 09:56.000
is one which allows him to drag one 
into his own mystery scenario.

09:56.000 --> 09:59.040
You can't get out until 
the mystery is solved.

09:59.360 --> 10:02.820
But this mystery is the scene 
of the Killing of Kindaichi.

10:02.820 --> 10:05.450
Which means, if I declare the facts,

10:05.450 --> 10:08.130
I can immediately return to 
my car in the real world.

10:08.130 --> 10:13.120
In other words, I can't be 
captured in this space.

10:13.120 --> 10:14.280
You're right.

10:14.860 --> 10:16.560
But you won't leave.

10:17.870 --> 10:20.590
Once you finish hearing me speak,

10:21.140 --> 10:22.450
you'll turn yourself in.

10:26.270 --> 10:33.110
<b>The
"Killing
of
Kindaichi"</b>

10:26.940 --> 10:28.720
The Killing of Kindaichi doesn't work

10:27.730 --> 10:33.110
<b>doesn't
work
if
the
author</b>

10:28.720 --> 10:33.110
if the author reveals the gimmick 
to anyone other than the murderer.

10:29.270 --> 10:33.110
<b>reveals
the
gimmick
to
anyone</b>

10:30.940 --> 10:33.110
<b>other
than
the
murderer.</b>

10:33.940 --> 10:37.210
In other words, the murderer 
had to have been unique.

10:37.730 --> 10:42.200
Which is why, at one point, I'd deduced 
that the motive was a personal grudge.

10:42.200 --> 10:44.150
But this is worse.

10:44.830 --> 10:48.860
To leave your escape as an afterthought to 
the murder is practically self-destruction.

10:49.560 --> 10:52.950
There are only two motivations one could 
have for driving a person to self-destruction.

10:53.320 --> 10:55.080
Insanity and duty.

10:56.680 --> 10:58.340
Take your pick, Yokomizo.

10:58.750 --> 11:01.730
Stabbing, poisoning, strangling or beating.

11:02.000 --> 11:03.230
How do you want it done?

11:04.780 --> 11:06.640
I'd have to say stabbing.

11:06.640 --> 11:10.400
Poisoning would require the reader 
to have a knowledge of chemistry.

11:10.400 --> 11:11.730
It wouldn't be fair.

11:11.730 --> 11:14.410
You filthy hack.

11:14.410 --> 11:17.290
No one's talking about your new novel.

11:17.290 --> 11:19.040
I'm talking about how I'm killing you.

11:19.040 --> 11:20.850
Oh. Sheesh.

11:20.850 --> 11:24.390
No, but seriously, give me some murder ideas.

11:24.390 --> 11:26.560
I'm not going to make 
my deadline this month.

11:26.560 --> 11:28.320
Here we go again.

11:28.670 --> 11:33.550
Mystery novels are just insider games that 
happen to be bound by external rules.

11:33.550 --> 11:36.580
Dying messages, gimmicks, enclosed spaces...

11:36.580 --> 11:38.790
They're completely detached from reality.

11:38.790 --> 11:41.840
If you want puzzles, go solve some 
math equations or something.

11:41.840 --> 11:46.570
Your distaste for mystery novels hasn't 
changed since we were in school.

11:46.570 --> 11:48.840
It's your fault I hate them.

11:49.220 --> 11:51.480
I get what you're saying, though.

11:51.480 --> 11:54.000
Meta-mysteries, anti-mysteries...

11:54.000 --> 11:57.030
No matter how unique a mystery 
you put out into the world,

11:57.030 --> 12:00.690
the next moment, it's just shoved 
into one category or another.

12:01.280 --> 12:04.830
The ultimate mystery can't exist.

12:06.210 --> 12:07.600
Nah. Anyway.

12:08.890 --> 12:11.630
It's been a long time since
 I've gotten to talk shop with you.

12:11.630 --> 12:13.180
I couldn't help but spill the beans.

12:13.950 --> 12:17.010
You always change the subject 
at the end of a debate.

12:17.010 --> 12:20.440
No wonder you've never had 
friends, even at school.

12:24.030 --> 12:27.300
You don't have friends, either.

12:27.950 --> 12:29.290
That's right.

12:29.290 --> 12:31.470
I killed him.

12:31.470 --> 12:34.300
I choked him to death with these hands.

12:34.300 --> 12:37.240
With bloodlust and madness.

12:37.240 --> 12:39.680
So, now what?

12:39.680 --> 12:41.880
The suspect has confessed to his crime.

12:41.880 --> 12:43.900
There's nothing you can...

12:43.900 --> 12:45.270
You never killed him.

12:46.280 --> 12:50.030
In the final chapter, the motive was 
described to be a personal grudge.

12:50.510 --> 12:52.210
That doesn't make sense, does it?

12:52.850 --> 12:54.910
If you were the one who'd killed him,

12:54.910 --> 12:57.540
not only would you have copied the 
plot gimmick, but the motive, as well.

12:58.750 --> 13:00.480
It's too perfect.

13:00.480 --> 13:03.470
It would practically be a script.

13:03.790 --> 13:07.450
The "Killing of Kindaichi" was a comedy that 
he both wrote and starred in himself.

13:08.170 --> 13:11.220
In other words, he killed himself.

13:12.050 --> 13:14.630
What a stupid way it turned out to be.

13:14.630 --> 13:16.490
But it was highly effective.

13:16.490 --> 13:18.610
Even people who don't read mystery novels

13:18.610 --> 13:21.240
became obsessed with the case 
and worked to solve it.

13:21.550 --> 13:26.210
The ultimate, uncategorizable, 
one-of-a-kind mystery.

13:26.210 --> 13:27.480
That's what this is.

13:27.820 --> 13:31.080
<b>"A mystery that leaks into the real world"</b>

13:28.120 --> 13:31.070
A mystery that leaks into the real world.

13:33.250 --> 13:35.740
I hate having regrets.

13:36.070 --> 13:39.110
That's why I've always done things my way.

13:39.110 --> 13:42.250
So far, I'm satisfied with my life.

13:42.920 --> 13:46.810
But now I find that I'm on limited time.

13:47.160 --> 13:50.840
Is your stomach really that messed up?

13:50.840 --> 13:52.510
I have a malignant tumor in my gut.

13:52.510 --> 13:54.370
I have a year at best, I was told.

13:55.190 --> 13:58.800
Before that, I'm going to complete 
the ultimate mystery novel.

13:59.350 --> 14:01.140
I've already finished my preparations.

14:01.700 --> 14:04.550
All except the key piece.

14:04.550 --> 14:06.240
And what key is that?

14:07.710 --> 14:08.860
The murderer.

14:10.520 --> 14:13.520
It would all be for nothing if it gets out 
that I'd done this myself prematurely.

14:13.980 --> 14:19.290
To avoid that, I need a real-life murderer 
who has actual motives and intent.

14:21.070 --> 14:23.240
I want you to be that person.

14:33.380 --> 14:35.260
Bingo!

14:35.260 --> 14:37.380
You nailed it, detective!

14:37.380 --> 14:40.220
I am indeed the role of 
the unhinged murderer!

14:41.140 --> 14:42.890
Of course I agreed!

14:42.890 --> 14:45.150
I'd get to kill the man I despised!

14:48.480 --> 14:52.150
On top of that, I get the money 
for selling the manuscript.

14:52.150 --> 14:54.320
Why would I ever refuse?!

14:54.690 --> 14:57.820
I killed him!

14:57.820 --> 15:01.240
Then why did you hide this 
page of the manuscript?

15:02.150 --> 15:06.910
Some of the words are smudged,
 including the word "End."

15:05.210 --> 15:09.710
<b>End</b>

15:06.910 --> 15:08.920
That must have occurred after 
the manuscript was completed.

15:09.480 --> 15:13.080
So, who made the smudges, and when?

15:13.080 --> 15:15.920
The stain happened during 
the crime or right after.

15:16.170 --> 15:18.940
The smudges marked the page in the 
reverse order in which it was completed.

15:18.940 --> 15:23.230
That is, it was with the 
final page placed on top.

15:23.230 --> 15:25.530
When you think of it that way, 
everything makes sense.

15:25.950 --> 15:27.010
Stop.

15:27.400 --> 15:30.370
The source of water at the scene of the crime,

15:31.190 --> 15:34.980
and the reason the attacker frantically tried 
to replace the original with a copy...

15:35.280 --> 15:39.110
When you put it all together, 
there can only be one explanation.

15:47.320 --> 15:51.740
Thank you... Mushi-kun...

15:51.740 --> 15:54.430
For taking this on...

15:55.150 --> 16:01.260
You truly... are my only...

16:05.770 --> 16:06.780
Tears.

16:09.760 --> 16:12.490
The perpetrator was crying 
as he strangled the victim.

16:12.900 --> 16:15.460
So if it wasn't motivated 
by a personal grudge,

16:15.460 --> 16:17.680
all the assumptions about the 
gimmick get turned over.

16:18.070 --> 16:20.490
If the victim was an accomplice to the crime,

16:20.490 --> 16:22.800
the very act of solving 
the crime is pointless.

16:23.380 --> 16:26.630
It isn't even a mystery, 
let alone the ultimate one.

16:27.480 --> 16:31.010
You realized as much just before 
you delivered the manuscript.

16:31.010 --> 16:32.890
That's why you replaced it with a photocopy.

16:33.670 --> 16:36.210
To fulfill your friend's final wish.

16:37.220 --> 16:38.830
You have no proof.

16:39.430 --> 16:40.800
You're right.

16:40.800 --> 16:43.770
Forensics could have determined 
that they were tears,

16:43.770 --> 16:46.290
but they couldn't determine whose they were.

16:46.840 --> 16:51.760
Still, it's enough to publicize the 
truth behind this manuscript.

16:52.160 --> 16:55.790
"It might have been a suicide. 
It might have been a farce."

16:55.790 --> 16:58.020
"It might be pointless to try to solve it."

16:58.850 --> 17:01.200
As soon the readers start to think that way,

17:01.200 --> 17:03.720
the value of taking on 
the challenge plummets,

17:03.720 --> 17:06.670
and your friend's final wish will be muddied.

17:09.330 --> 17:11.910
The Detective Agency was 
once defeated by Fyodor.

17:13.290 --> 17:14.950
We won't be defeated again.

17:14.950 --> 17:17.420
I won't let you hurt anyone in the Agency.

17:17.420 --> 17:18.870
<i>What is this?</i>

17:18.870 --> 17:21.430
To that end, I memorized and assimilated...

17:22.740 --> 17:24.640
the demon himself!

17:25.630 --> 17:28.850
If you don't turn yourself in, 
I'll go public with that hypothesis.

17:28.850 --> 17:30.350
This isn't detective work.

17:30.840 --> 17:33.680
It's a demonic mind control 
invading your mind.

17:34.000 --> 17:38.340
My new weapon for killing Detective killers!

17:47.950 --> 17:48.910
No...

17:50.250 --> 17:52.060
I can't allow that.

17:53.090 --> 17:54.540
Please don't make it public.

17:56.050 --> 17:58.590
I despise Yokomizo.

17:59.270 --> 18:01.820
It's not possible that I don't.

18:04.580 --> 18:06.010
I'll turn myself in.

18:10.810 --> 18:11.760
Yeah.

18:11.760 --> 18:12.880
I see.

18:12.880 --> 18:13.850
All right.

18:15.100 --> 18:17.680
We have evidence that grenades

18:17.680 --> 18:20.730
of the type used by the Detective Agency 
were stolen in transport.

18:21.080 --> 18:24.720
That makes it likely that they were 
used in the murder of the girl.

18:24.720 --> 18:26.860
He released his special ability.

18:27.260 --> 18:29.630
Kunikida will be released.

18:29.630 --> 18:30.730
Rampo-kun.

18:31.840 --> 18:34.270
About the dummy corpse...

18:34.270 --> 18:37.430
There wasn't any biological activity 
detected in the wound on his face.

18:37.430 --> 18:38.210
Oh.

18:38.590 --> 18:42.360
He just threw a corpse that Fyodor gave him.

18:42.360 --> 18:46.110
I doubt he's ever killed anyone 
other than the mystery novelist.

18:47.720 --> 18:48.880
Rampo-kun?

18:53.480 --> 18:55.350
I don't want to bother throwing it out.

18:55.350 --> 18:56.200
You can have it.

18:57.380 --> 18:58.420
What's this?

18:59.220 --> 19:01.540
An employee ID?

19:01.540 --> 19:05.310
That company is a front for an 
anti-government organization.

19:05.960 --> 19:08.580
A Gifted Special Ops Division 
agent working undercover there

19:08.580 --> 19:11.700
is about to have their cover blown.

19:11.700 --> 19:12.830
Go help them.

19:13.400 --> 19:15.090
Why are you asking me?

19:15.420 --> 19:19.540
That agent is also in charge 
of hiring at the Division.

19:20.930 --> 19:24.330
I couldn't care less what 
happens to the agent,

19:24.330 --> 19:28.550
but if they learn about your powerful ability, 
they'll be obliged to hire you.

19:29.190 --> 19:30.830
Go show them what you can do.

19:31.320 --> 19:32.480
Rampo-kun...

19:33.160 --> 19:34.270
Are you...

19:34.270 --> 19:36.350
I promised, didn't I?

19:36.350 --> 19:39.280
That I'd help you find work 
if you ever needed it.

19:41.050 --> 19:44.740
Mushi-kun, I bet you'd laugh at me

19:45.490 --> 19:50.000
for trying to master mystery novels, 
even if it means sacrificing myself.

19:50.720 --> 19:53.060
But when you start going down that path,

19:53.060 --> 19:56.130
you realize there really is nothing 
whose value is immutable.

19:57.010 --> 19:59.170
Huh? Where'd my lighter go?

19:59.170 --> 20:01.680
In which case, it's up to you to choose.

20:02.940 --> 20:05.640
Choose what you consider 
valuable in your life.

20:06.720 --> 20:10.090
After all, the greatest luxury 
afforded to a human being

20:10.550 --> 20:14.790
is the right to make the 
world itself their choice.

20:23.650 --> 20:24.580
What the...

20:25.570 --> 20:26.640
An accident?

20:31.540 --> 20:32.730
Is it an accident?

20:32.730 --> 20:34.410
It's a murder.

20:34.410 --> 20:35.410
Who's the victim?

20:35.850 --> 20:36.920
You.

20:42.440 --> 20:45.950
<i>A gun just appeared out of thin air!</i>

20:49.050 --> 20:50.360
Now, then...

20:50.360 --> 20:53.840
It's quiz time!

20:56.720 --> 20:59.810
Who might I be?

21:00.830 --> 21:01.990
What?

21:01.990 --> 21:03.990
My name's Nikolai, you say?

21:03.990 --> 21:06.260
That's right!

21:06.260 --> 21:08.530
Okay, next question!

21:08.530 --> 21:11.030
Why am I here?

21:11.630 --> 21:13.500
Hint: Cleanup duty.

21:14.070 --> 21:16.210
Oops, I gave away the answer!

21:16.520 --> 21:17.910
Cleanup duty?

21:17.910 --> 21:19.100
That's right.

21:19.100 --> 21:24.290
My duty is to get rid of those 
who know of our next project.

21:24.290 --> 21:27.850
A quiz is no fun if someone gives 
away the answer, after all.

21:30.570 --> 21:32.030
"Our"?

21:32.030 --> 21:34.280
So you're with Fyodor!

21:34.280 --> 21:35.560
Indeed!

21:35.560 --> 21:38.420
We are the Decay of the Angels!

21:38.420 --> 21:40.980
Terrorists lurking in this land!

21:41.460 --> 21:44.290
The five angels, here to tell 
of the end of the gods' world!

21:48.170 --> 21:49.030
<i>Rampo-kun!</i>

21:49.030 --> 21:50.010
<i>Listen up!</i>

21:50.010 --> 21:52.490
<i>The Detective Agency is about
 to get a huge job offer!</i>

21:52.490 --> 21:54.070
<i>Don't accept it!</i>

21:54.070 --> 21:56.340
<i>If you do, it'll be the end of the Agency!</i>

21:56.340 --> 21:57.410
<i>You hear me?</i>

21:57.410 --> 21:58.720
<i>Don't you dare accept—</i>

23:37.730 --> 23:40.010
<i>Tragic Sunday</i>

23:37.730 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode: 43
